WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.091
I love my digital art,

00:00:01.091 --> 00:00:03.898
but I want to take it with&nbsp;
me out into the real world.

00:00:03.898 --> 00:00:05.219
Thankfully we can access

00:00:05.219 --> 00:00:07.771
augmented reality on 
our mobile devices.

00:00:07.771 --> 00:00:10.739
We could use this tool 
to simply cover the world.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:12.559
Or we could use it 

00:00:12.559 --> 00:00:14.571
to further connect
 us to this&nbsp;world.

00:00:14.571 --> 00:00:16.456
We had a lot of artists 
reaching out to us,

00:00:16.456 --> 00:00:17.739
so we created tools

00:00:17.739 --> 00:00:19.231
to allow them to&nbsp;
augment their work.

00:00:19.231 --> 00:00:21.148
And very quickly, we 
had a community

00:00:21.148 --> 00:00:23.630
of artists covering the world&nbsp;
with their augmented art.

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:24.714
It was beautiful.

00:00:24.714 --> 00:00:25.905
This is just the beginning.

00:00:25.905 --> 00:00:28.512
You could leave a digital&nbsp;
artwork on the street corner

00:00:28.512 --> 00:00:30.178
for your lover to find.

00:00:30.178 --> 00:00:31.771
You could reinvent 
your backyard

00:00:31.771 --> 00:00:33.140
with an&nbsp;animated 
treasure hunt

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:35.287
for your kids and their friends.

00:00:35.287 --> 00:00:36.721
The digital worlds we build

00:00:36.721 --> 00:00:39.897
can be a&nbsp;wonderful playground 
for exploring identity,

00:00:39.897 --> 00:00:43.281
for learning new skills, 
for practicing&nbsp;creativity

00:00:43.281 --> 00:00:45.253
and bringing our 
communities together.

